      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"step-q82720\" class=\"step questionWidget\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 2</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\"><p>Simplify the following sentence: \"The pen is blue and it is a blue pen, or the pen is blue or it is a red pen.\"</p>\n</div><table class=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82720-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\"> The pen is red.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82720-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\"> The pen is blue or red.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82720-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\"> The pen is blue or red but not both.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82720-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\"> The pen is blue and red.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82720-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">The pen is blue.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/incorrect-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectText\">Incorrect</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p></p><p>First, we simplify the phrase \"the pen is blue and it is a blue pen\" to just \"the pen is blue.\" The sentence now reads</p><p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The pen is blue, or the pen is blue or it is a red pen.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Then, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The pen is blue or the pen is blue, or it is a red pen.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Now, we simplify the phrase \"the pen is blue or the pen is blue\" to just \"the pen is blue.\" The sentence now reads</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The pen is blue, or it is a red pen.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Finally, we simplify the sentence to</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The pen is blue or red.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div></div>",
