      "problem": "Simplify $(M∧N)∧(N∨N).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the associative and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(M∧N)∧(N∨N) & ≡(M∧N)∧N \\\\  & ≡M∧(N∧N) \\\\  & ≡M∧N.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
